     1	"""Cost estimate of the churn replication (plan draft 3, review r3 caveats applied) from experiments/v2/benchmark/timings.json, the churn slowdown
     2	measured for the churn arm (docs/revision/churn/churn_cost.py) and the memory-safe worker counts of the churn arm and
     3	Run B. Two numbers per scenario: core-hours at 0.108 USD per core-hour, and billed pod time from a stage schedule
     4	(waves at the stage's worker limit, stages in sequence) at 0.56 USD per hour; the estimate is the larger of the two.
     5	Assumptions are named inline; review round 1 asked for the schedule, the gates, calibration, diagnostics, continuation
